WEBVTT

01:27.140 --> 01:29.980
AQUARION

01:33.200 --> 01:34.500
This is...

01:34.950 --> 01:36.580
a robot, right?

01:36.800 --> 01:39.430
They never taught us about this.

01:41.090 --> 01:42.410
The Mechanical Angel...

01:43.960 --> 01:45.230
Aquarion.

01:46.750 --> 01:51.840
Unbelievable! Those three fused
and turned into Aquarion?

01:51.840 --> 01:54.440
That mysterious agency
with the Vector Machines

01:54.440 --> 01:56.550
must have been working toward this!

01:59.350 --> 02:00.050
Here it comes!

02:00.050 --> 02:00.980
Okay.

02:02.970 --> 02:03.970
Take this!

02:05.630 --> 02:06.770
You got it!

02:07.480 --> 02:11.860
It seems that the Vector Siegel pilot,
Otori-kun, is controlling it right now.

02:12.390 --> 02:15.820
No, the three of them are
controlling it together.

02:17.190 --> 02:18.250
Now's our chance!

02:18.250 --> 02:19.180
Yeah!

02:20.270 --> 02:21.920
Yes! A double punch!

02:21.920 --> 02:22.870
I'm here, too.

02:22.870 --> 02:23.660
Yeah!

02:23.660 --> 02:24.880
Let's back off.

02:26.240 --> 02:27.910
Or make it think we are!

02:27.910 --> 02:29.380
And then a triple kick!

02:29.380 --> 02:31.780
Aquarion, triple kick!

02:33.450 --> 02:35.430
Oh! Hey, come back here!

02:35.430 --> 02:36.710
Don't go after it!

02:37.320 --> 02:38.460
Ugh.

02:37.320 --> 02:38.460
Phew.

02:42.070 --> 02:44.570
Did you see those things fly off?

02:44.570 --> 02:46.970
They're probably the Space
Preservation Agency's new mecha units.

02:46.970 --> 02:51.400
I guess Enoshima really is a
Preservation Agency base.

02:51.400 --> 02:51.990
Oh.

02:51.990 --> 02:52.920
Huh?

02:53.430 --> 02:55.030
They came back.

03:02.510 --> 03:04.110
What is this place?

03:05.300 --> 03:06.340
Guys!

03:09.720 --> 03:13.080
I'm so glad that you're all safe!

03:12.320 --> 03:13.920
Mm-hmm.

03:14.320 --> 03:17.100
Sensei, what is this place?

03:17.100 --> 03:21.220
It's the Space Preservation
Agency's Enoshima base.

03:21.220 --> 03:24.590
So those rumors about a
secret base were true.

03:24.590 --> 03:28.650
And this is the organic
quantum computer, DEAVA.

03:29.020 --> 03:32.200
She's the one who chose you as Elements.

03:32.200 --> 03:35.260
DEAVA... like a god.

03:35.260 --> 03:40.110
I think you know by now, but the reason you
were chosen was to fight those things.

03:40.410 --> 03:41.720
Aquarion.

03:42.510 --> 03:44.830
Oh, right. I heard a voice.

03:44.830 --> 03:46.450
What the heck is that thing anyway?

03:46.680 --> 03:50.640
A legendary Mechanical Angel that is said
to have knowledge of heaven and earth.

03:50.640 --> 03:52.960
Knowledge of heaven and earth...

03:52.960 --> 03:57.920
It is the ultimate weapon that
we have been searching for.

03:58.210 --> 04:03.870
We want to use Aquarion's powers to
protect our universe with your help.

04:06.420 --> 04:08.330
So what are you gonna do?

04:08.330 --> 04:09.160
About what?

04:09.160 --> 04:11.550
Piloting Aquarion or not.

04:11.550 --> 04:15.210
Munakata-sensei said we have
to decide by ourselves.

04:16.340 --> 04:18.650
They always use the same trick.

04:18.650 --> 04:21.570
That make it our responsibility.
Like, "You're the one who chose to do this."

04:21.570 --> 04:23.070
Huh?

04:23.070 --> 04:25.090
Because we were in primary school.

04:25.090 --> 04:26.890
Oh, the scout class.

04:26.890 --> 04:30.410
But doesn't everyone want to
get into the elite class?

04:30.410 --> 04:34.160
In our case, we were sold off.
By our parents.

04:34.360 --> 04:35.460
Huh?

04:35.460 --> 04:38.930
Well, at least that's what I always thought.

04:39.480 --> 04:44.180
When I was a kid, I took some kind
of national test in preschool.

04:44.660 --> 04:47.150
I guess I got a pretty good score.

04:47.150 --> 04:49.190
And then some people in
suits came to see me.

04:51.170 --> 04:53.970
They said something about gathering
all the high-scoring kids

04:53.970 --> 04:57.380
and having them participate in an
experimental education program.

04:58.350 --> 05:00.720
At first, there were maybe thirty of us.

05:01.400 --> 05:05.470
They put us in a place that looked like a hospital
and made us do all sorts of experiments.

05:05.470 --> 05:08.810
Soon kids dropped out.
First one, then another.

05:09.320 --> 05:11.440
I don't know what their standards were,

05:11.850 --> 05:15.060
but Sayo and I were among
the kids that remained.

05:15.060 --> 05:17.870
Momohime was there too,
one year older than us.

05:17.870 --> 05:20.510
Momohime-sama? I'm so jelly.

05:21.030 --> 05:24.650
They kept this quiet, but some
kids who dropped out ended up,

05:24.650 --> 05:27.840
I don't know, kind of broken or something.

05:27.840 --> 05:29.770
What do you mean? What was broken?

05:30.380 --> 05:31.440
Their hearts.

05:31.900 --> 05:36.070
Anyway, that's when I stopped trusting them.

05:36.070 --> 05:38.220
Schools and teachers, I mean.

05:38.220 --> 05:41.250
And started getting in trouble
for bad behavior, huh.

05:41.250 --> 05:43.420
Rimiya-kun, you don't need to be so blunt.

05:43.420 --> 05:45.950
Then are you going to quit
being an Element, Sakko?

05:46.740 --> 05:49.030
Look, do you remember...

05:49.030 --> 05:49.960
Hm?

05:50.430 --> 05:52.870
I mean, did you feel something?

05:52.870 --> 05:54.240
What was that?

05:54.240 --> 05:59.370
Dunno. Kind of like a new emotion, I guess.

06:00.290 --> 06:02.940
Sorry, I'm going home this way. See you.

06:02.940 --> 06:04.060
Uh...

06:06.660 --> 06:07.910
Huh?

06:11.270 --> 06:13.670
He's at it again?

06:17.880 --> 06:21.820
The Space Preservation Agency
has spent many years

06:21.820 --> 06:24.890
preparing for an invasion from mythic space.

06:25.260 --> 06:28.290
It all began with a set of clay
tablets that were discovered

06:28.290 --> 06:31.150
in a secret archive, hidden deep
within a certain set of ruins.

06:31.440 --> 06:35.460
These texts, known as the Naacal Tablets,
contain myths about the creation of the world

06:35.460 --> 06:38.040
and details about ancient
super-civilizations.

06:38.460 --> 06:42.140
That myth system was also
a kind of philosophy.

06:42.140 --> 06:43.590
A theory of the universe.

06:44.350 --> 06:49.020
It's just like what modern science
might call a multiverse theory.

06:50.320 --> 06:55.130
Remember how I taught you space can be split
into two via a double-slit experiment?

06:55.130 --> 06:59.750
Still, considering the absolute volume of
the universe, it would be more economical

06:59.750 --> 07:02.580
to pretend that those trivial
differences don't exist.

07:02.580 --> 07:07.620
The power of the universe to negate such
a split, almost like healing a wound,

07:07.620 --> 07:10.330
is what we call the universe's
ability to self-correct.

07:11.360 --> 07:14.090
The cat may be alive or dead,

07:14.090 --> 07:17.240
but both realities can be incorporated
into the universe without contradiction.

07:17.800 --> 07:21.980
Research into the Naacal Tablets was begun
in secret by international organizations

07:21.980 --> 07:24.460
and predates the Space Preservation Agency.

07:24.800 --> 07:27.540
And then, here in the
underground caverns of Enoshima,

07:27.540 --> 07:31.880
we found wreckage of vehicles that incorporate
the power of that ancient civilization.

07:32.420 --> 07:36.780
We were able to revive them using
the power of modern science,

07:36.780 --> 07:38.890
but we still hadn't uncovered
their true function.

07:39.890 --> 07:43.000
The Naacal Tablets contain a warning

07:43.000 --> 07:47.140
to use those vehicles to prepare for an
eventual invasion from mythic space.

07:47.310 --> 07:48.910
Mythic space?

07:49.180 --> 07:53.130
The realm of monsters that have
been driven out of our universe.

07:53.130 --> 07:55.030
The universe of the Shadow Angels.

07:55.880 --> 08:01.200
The monsters' universe, which split
off roughly 12,000 years ago,

08:01.200 --> 08:04.400
is connected to our universe
at the quantum level.

08:04.730 --> 08:08.680
And right now, it is trying to
fuse with our universe again.

08:08.970 --> 08:12.540
When that happens, the differences
between the universes will cancel out,

08:12.540 --> 08:17.280
and just as the violation of CP-symmetry
erased dark matter right after the big bang,

08:17.280 --> 08:22.640
the larger space—even if it is only
slightly so—will eliminate the other one.

08:23.380 --> 08:27.030
The Mythic Beasts will try
to expand their territory

08:27.030 --> 08:30.700
in order to eliminate our universe.

08:31.000 --> 08:35.210
Our last hope for staving off that
threat is the Mechanical Angel,

08:35.760 --> 08:36.940
Aquarion.

09:02.050 --> 09:04.050
Oh, Munakata-sensei.

09:04.050 --> 09:06.650
Is something up with Munakata-chi, Momo?

09:06.650 --> 09:08.020
I don't know.

09:08.020 --> 09:09.160
What do you mean?

09:09.160 --> 09:13.920
I don't know, but I have a feeling she knows
something about what happened to Sayo.

09:13.920 --> 09:17.620
Sayo? You mean that second-year girl you
were friends with? The one who died?

09:17.620 --> 09:19.170
I'll go ask her.

09:22.190 --> 09:23.620
Munakata-sensei!

09:23.960 --> 09:24.960
Huh?

09:29.230 --> 09:31.490
The higher-ups have been waiting.

09:31.490 --> 09:36.380
We, the members of the World Awakening
Council, talked about Aquarion.

09:36.380 --> 09:39.490
It was fortunate that we discovered
the legendary Mechanical Angel.

09:39.490 --> 09:40.850
Even then, however,

09:40.850 --> 09:43.770
we were still unable
to defeat the Mythic Beast.

09:44.000 --> 09:46.730
How is it that you weren't even
aware the Vector Machines

09:46.730 --> 09:49.140
could fuse and become Aquarion?

09:49.140 --> 09:53.240
When fused, the internal structure
of the Machines changes completely,

09:53.240 --> 09:55.800
into something almost like
an organic life form.

09:56.040 --> 09:57.900
I've never seen anything like it.

09:57.900 --> 10:00.840
When the Sun, the Moon,
and Mercury are in alignment,

10:00.840 --> 10:03.030
the melody of a new fusion
begins to resonate.

10:03.360 --> 10:07.900
It may be what the line in the
Naacal Tablets is referring to.

10:07.900 --> 10:10.200
How are the Elements doing?

10:10.200 --> 10:12.460
I was able to deliver my lectures.

10:12.460 --> 10:15.210
I expect they're searching
their conscience right now.

10:15.210 --> 10:17.240
Regarding the Elements,

10:17.240 --> 10:19.810
are you certain that you have recruited
the best possible candidates?

10:19.810 --> 10:24.300
They were chosen by DEAVA,
so there's no question.

10:24.300 --> 10:27.500
The organic quantum computer we developed

10:27.500 --> 10:31.930
gives oracles based on logic
that even we don't understand.

10:31.930 --> 10:35.390
But right now, it's the only thing
we have to depend on.

10:35.390 --> 10:37.440
Take care of things, you two.

10:38.830 --> 10:40.700
Just as expected.

10:48.560 --> 10:52.310
I'll say this one more time, but you don't
have to do this if you don't want to.

10:52.310 --> 10:56.820
This universe might be destroyed if
you don't, but I cannot force you.

10:57.860 --> 10:58.960
Ichiki-san?

10:59.480 --> 11:01.220
I'll do it.

11:01.630 --> 11:02.840
Sayo?

11:02.840 --> 11:07.790
I always want to do whatever
I can to be helpful.

11:07.790 --> 11:11.220
If the job is protecting all the
people of the world, I'll do it.

11:12.740 --> 11:13.730
Hatano-kun?

11:13.730 --> 11:15.810
Please ask me last.

11:16.170 --> 11:17.230
Tsukishiro-kun?

11:17.230 --> 11:19.060
I guess I don't mind.

11:19.480 --> 11:21.620
Okay. And you, Otori-kun?

11:22.100 --> 11:25.110
Yeah, I'll do it.
I know I can't say no anyway.

11:25.110 --> 11:27.760
Weren't you listening?
You are free to say no.

11:28.240 --> 11:29.510
But still, thank you.

11:30.200 --> 11:31.630
Finally, Hatano-kun?

11:32.550 --> 11:36.250
If everyone else is doing it,
then I will, too.

11:38.050 --> 11:40.480
Kind of pisses you off, right?

11:40.480 --> 11:41.570
Does it?

11:41.570 --> 11:46.700
But I'm actually pretty serious.
I don't mind doing it.

11:46.700 --> 11:47.640
Toshi...

11:47.980 --> 11:52.570
My mom was so excited when
I got accepted to this school.

11:53.190 --> 11:57.900
I think you all know that
I always got the worst grades.

11:57.900 --> 12:01.240
I was never into studying
the way everyone else was.

12:01.770 --> 12:03.910
It just didn't stick for me.

12:03.910 --> 12:07.160
So that's why you're always
studying like crazy.

12:07.910 --> 12:10.350
That's gotta be a pain.

12:11.430 --> 12:16.670
What Ichiki-san said made me
realize that I lack a heart.

12:17.510 --> 12:23.320
But if someone like that can still protect
the world, it makes me a little happy.

12:23.680 --> 12:27.900
Well for me it's a little different,
Toshi, but I don't mind doing it either.

12:28.280 --> 12:33.310
I think I probably lack something, too.
But then when that happened,

12:33.580 --> 12:35.790
this feeling came over me.

12:36.560 --> 12:39.410
It was like the empty part
of me was being tickled.

12:39.410 --> 12:41.150
It was a really weird feeling.

12:41.990 --> 12:44.820
I just wanted to feel that way again.

12:45.090 --> 12:46.970
Yeah, good point.

12:49.230 --> 12:51.740
I didn't know this could
connect to the Escar.

12:53.410 --> 12:57.130
By the way, we forgot to
ask about Ichiki-san.

12:57.130 --> 12:58.230
Yeah.

12:58.230 --> 13:02.080
Back in primary school,
Sayo and I were in the same club.

13:02.080 --> 13:03.080
Club?

13:03.080 --> 13:04.960
The dismantling club.

13:04.960 --> 13:08.090
A weird club where we took things
apart to see how they worked.

13:08.430 --> 13:11.230
And there were only three members.

13:11.630 --> 13:14.350
It was me, Sayo, and Momohime,
who was a year older.

13:14.620 --> 13:16.130
Momohime-sama?

13:16.350 --> 13:18.260
She's the one who started the club.

13:19.820 --> 13:21.750
Sayo was a lot like me.

13:21.750 --> 13:25.220
Ever since I was a kid,
I was never afraid of anything,

13:25.220 --> 13:27.660
so I was always doing
really dangerous stuff.

13:28.380 --> 13:31.620
She never thought about
her own safety either.

13:31.620 --> 13:33.210
We were always doing risky stuff,

13:33.210 --> 13:36.260
so Momohime basically
had to watch out for us.

13:36.260 --> 13:39.330
We collected all this junk and took it apart.

13:39.330 --> 13:43.260
It was a lot of fun at first,
but I started getting bored after a while.

13:43.260 --> 13:48.460
Hey, it's boring if we just dismantle stuff.
Let's build something with these parts.

13:48.460 --> 13:49.590
A robot or something!

13:49.590 --> 13:50.760
That sounds fun!

13:51.040 --> 13:51.970
Yeah!

13:52.900 --> 13:55.550
I guess we wanted to keep it secret,

13:55.550 --> 13:59.950
so we hid in a cave on the other side of the
island and put it together there. Then...

14:01.420 --> 14:03.520
Why are you putting a flower on it?

14:03.520 --> 14:05.400
It's a nice carnation!

14:05.400 --> 14:06.860
Do you remember, Momo-chan?

14:06.860 --> 14:11.030
A long time ago, you told me
I was like a carnation.

14:11.030 --> 14:12.380
Sure I do!

14:12.620 --> 14:16.710
In class, we had to compare ourselves to
something and I didn't know what to say.

14:16.710 --> 14:20.370
You whispered to me and said,
"You're like a carnation, Sayo."

14:20.780 --> 14:24.890
It just popped into my head.
It's my favorite flower.

14:24.890 --> 14:27.540
Then I started liking carnations, too.

14:28.610 --> 14:30.380
What should we name it?

14:30.380 --> 14:31.160
Churo.

14:31.160 --> 14:32.320
What kind of name is that?

14:32.320 --> 14:34.590
It's the name of a mythological warrior.

14:34.590 --> 14:36.840
Okay. Here we go!

14:37.260 --> 14:40.590
Mythic Hero Churo! Activate!

14:42.960 --> 14:46.230
Starting. Starting. Reset.

14:46.760 --> 14:47.960
Huh?

14:46.760 --> 14:50.160
Space, fusion, annihilation!

14:48.420 --> 14:49.840
Aah!

14:50.410 --> 14:53.900
Space, fusion, annihilation!

14:51.990 --> 14:54.540
Dismantling
Safety Is Number One

14:54.540 --> 14:57.550
Space, fusion, annihilation!

15:00.660 --> 15:01.590
Hey!

15:02.050 --> 15:03.240
Sakko!

15:03.990 --> 15:05.160
Be careful!

15:04.430 --> 15:07.760
Space, fusion, annihilation!

15:06.720 --> 15:07.760
Sayo!

15:08.370 --> 15:11.400
Space, fusion, annihilation!

15:15.140 --> 15:16.720
Space, fusion—

15:18.690 --> 15:23.100
One way we were different was that although
Sayo never thought about her own safety,

15:23.100 --> 15:27.240
when she saw someone else in danger,
she would risk her life to help them.

15:27.240 --> 15:30.150
That night of the funeral,
I suddenly remembered it.

15:30.940 --> 15:32.230
The carnation.

15:33.230 --> 15:37.240
But the next day, they didn't say
anything about that on the news at all.

15:37.240 --> 15:40.910
They said it was a random act of
violence, committed by a person.

15:40.910 --> 15:41.840
Huh?

15:42.360 --> 15:46.750
The people who witnessed it didn't
remember the robot, either.

15:47.260 --> 15:51.530
We even started to wonder if it had
all been a dream or something.

15:52.210 --> 15:58.260
Then we dismantled the dismantling club
and the three of us slowly drifted apart.

15:58.540 --> 16:01.320
That's the universe's ability to self-correct.

16:01.320 --> 16:02.110
Huh?

16:02.110 --> 16:03.040
Whoa!

16:03.320 --> 16:04.360
She appeared again!

16:05.320 --> 16:08.960
Hey, Sakko, do you want
to go back to that cave?

16:08.960 --> 16:11.990
But it's off-limits after what happened.

16:11.990 --> 16:13.870
That doesn't matter. Let's go.

16:29.580 --> 16:31.460
What do you make of this?

16:31.460 --> 16:32.460
Hmm.

16:33.710 --> 16:34.930
Look, it's still here.

16:36.080 --> 16:37.530
I still remember.

16:40.750 --> 16:45.570
They say the universe's ability to self-correct
can work forward and backward in time.

16:48.020 --> 16:53.310
Even in a universe where a person's life and
death can coexist without contradiction,

16:53.310 --> 16:57.250
if you move forward or backward enough,
you end up dead anyway, right?

17:00.970 --> 17:03.510
Did I die?

17:05.120 --> 17:08.030
They said your last words were,
"I don't want to die."

17:08.030 --> 17:08.980
Rimiya!

17:08.980 --> 17:09.910
Hmm?

17:12.880 --> 17:16.540
Yeah? Thank you, Rimiya-kun.

17:17.650 --> 17:19.430
It's the crack from before!

17:19.430 --> 17:20.930
The same thing is coming out!

17:20.930 --> 17:23.210
Munakata-sensei, please contact the kids.

17:23.210 --> 17:24.140
All right.

17:25.460 --> 17:28.900
Thank goodness. They're right nearby.

17:38.860 --> 17:40.370
A Mythic Beast has appeared.

17:40.370 --> 17:42.590
I need the four of you immediately.
I'll open a gate.

17:42.590 --> 17:43.520
Huh?

17:45.590 --> 17:47.240
We can go from here?

17:47.240 --> 17:50.530
Hurry up! You're launching with
the same team as last time.

17:51.440 --> 17:53.770
If the universe does have the
ability to correct itself,

17:53.770 --> 17:55.980
then we can find a way
to correct your future.

17:55.980 --> 17:56.910
He's right!

18:00.470 --> 18:03.560
As long as you don't deploy with us,
at least you won't die.

18:03.560 --> 18:06.720
From now on, we'll always protect you.

18:14.520 --> 18:17.210
Vector Machines, all units take off!

18:18.040 --> 18:20.330
Vector Siegel, launch!

18:23.770 --> 18:26.260
Vector Feoh, launch!

18:28.720 --> 18:31.090
Vector Tir, launch!

18:36.130 --> 18:37.470
Here we go!

18:37.470 --> 18:38.280
Okay!

18:38.280 --> 18:39.210
Yeah!

18:43.820 --> 18:47.010
Mythic Star Fusion! Go, Aquarion!

18:48.970 --> 18:52.060
You can't! The mana gauge hasn't
reached fusion level yet!

18:52.760 --> 18:54.260
Whoa!

18:53.140 --> 18:54.260
Toshi!

18:54.260 --> 18:56.840
He's okay. I switched him to autopilot.

18:58.140 --> 18:59.700
But at this rate...

18:59.970 --> 19:05.370
Yeah. With his emotions shut off,
his unit won't be able to join in the attack.

19:05.610 --> 19:06.570
Sensei!

19:06.570 --> 19:07.540
Ichiki-san?

19:07.540 --> 19:08.920
I'll go.

19:09.410 --> 19:12.940
All right. Saruta-sensei, teleport her.

19:14.960 --> 19:16.510
Okay.

19:19.980 --> 19:21.450
This isn't gonna work!

19:21.450 --> 19:23.670
Rimiya-kun, go right!

19:24.600 --> 19:25.570
Did you...

19:25.570 --> 19:27.780
Now's your chance! Unite your feelings!

19:30.320 --> 19:33.350
The gauge has reached
fusion level! Go for it!

19:33.640 --> 19:35.140
Mythic Star Fusion!

19:35.140 --> 19:37.150
Go, Aquarion!

19:53.120 --> 19:56.590
What's happening?
It wasn't like this before.

20:00.740 --> 20:03.970
Ah, this feels so nice.

20:12.140 --> 20:13.190
Let's go!

20:13.650 --> 20:14.580
Yeah!

20:18.370 --> 20:20.450
Don't! You're too exposed!

20:21.740 --> 20:25.340
That was close!
I keep losing all sense of fear.

20:25.340 --> 20:28.920
Don't worry. I'll be scared for you instead.

20:28.920 --> 20:29.850
Sayo...

20:30.440 --> 20:31.950
Sakko, behind us!

20:34.760 --> 20:35.880
No!

20:45.580 --> 20:48.950
Sakko, now's your chance!

20:49.810 --> 20:52.470
Sayo!

20:52.980 --> 20:57.680
Aquarion! Infinite Despair Punch!

20:59.690 --> 21:02.150
Infinite Despair Punch

21:21.710 --> 21:24.800
You did it, Sakko.

21:24.800 --> 21:26.690
Sayo! Hold on!

21:27.310 --> 21:29.460
I finally understood.

21:30.040 --> 21:34.910
This is what it feels like
to care about yourself.

21:36.080 --> 21:41.140
I don't... want to die.

21:43.170 --> 21:47.940
And in that moment, I remembered...

21:49.440 --> 21:52.170
about when I went to pick that flower.

21:53.090 --> 21:56.420
She was honestly kind of a
weird girl, that Ichiki-san.
